sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant L as Home laptop
    participant T as Stable tunnel provider
    participant C as ChatGPT
    participant M as Authenticated local MCP gateway
    participant D as Desktop Commander stdio child

    L->>M: Start loopback Streamable HTTP adapter
    L->>T: Reconnect outbound tunnel using saved identity
    T-->>L: Restore same public HTTPS hostname
    U->>C: Configure custom MCP app once with fixed /mcp URL
    C->>M: OAuth / authorization through tunnel
    M-->>C: Authorized MCP transport
    C->>M: MCP call using permitted remote tool
    M->>M: Enforce remote allowlist/policy
    M->>D: MCP request over stdio
    D-->>M: Result
    M-->>C: MCP result

    Note over L,C: Network/IP changes do not require reconfiguration while public identity is preserved
    Note over L,C: Selected arguments/results can leave the laptop; source execution remains local
    Note over L,C: Sleep/offline preserves configuration identity, not availability
